From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:16:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 199/342] usb_webcam: frame sizes as asked, MJPEG through
 libjpeg-turbo (M45)

The UVC device keeps a mode per frame descriptor of YUY2 or MJPEG, with
the frame interval closest to 30 frames a second, and takes the size a
connection asks for: YUY2 where it is as fast as MJPEG (on the C920 up
to 640x480), else MJPEG. A size left open gets 640x480, else 320x240.
The probe asks for the mode's format, frame and interval.

MJPEG frames go to two decoder threads that take them in turn and decode
into their own buffers with libjpeg-turbo (TurboJPEG, NEON, to B_RGB32);
the newest whole frame becomes the ready one, which FillFrameBuffer()
copies. A 1080p frame of the C920 takes a Cortex-A53 37 ms, 720p 18 ms.
Built only with the turbojpeg build feature; without it, YUY2 as before.

The deframer takes MJPEG frames up to the probe's maximum size. The
producer no longer forces 320x240, answers raw video format suggestions
(it refused all but encoded video), fills in bytes_per_row, sizes its
buffer group by the frame (8 buffers, 4 of a 1080p frame), restarts a
running stream on a new connection, and sends nothing when no frame
came.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
